.TH LIBMPQ__WRITER_TIMESTAMP 3 2026-09-10 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__writer_timestamp \- set an explicit FILETIME on an MPQ file writer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__writer_timestamp("
.BI "        mpq_writer_s *" "writer,"
.BI "        uint64_t " "filetime"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Set the timestamp of an active file writer before
\fBlibmpq__writer_finish\fP(). The archive must enable
LIBMPQ_ATTRIBUTE_FILETIME in options.attributes.
.PP
\fIfiletime\fP is a Windows FILETIME: an unsigned count of 100-nanosecond
ticks since 1601-01-01 UTC, not Unix time. Zero is the default.
No filesystem timestamp is imported by \fBlibmpq__archive_add_path\fP().
This call neither changes the source file nor creates a patch.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP after setting the active writer's FILETIME,
or a negative libmpq error. The call does not consume the writer.
.SH ERRORS
NULL writers return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP; an inactive writer returns
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP; disabled FILETIME generation returns
\fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT\fP.
